Here is the structured goal model for the mission:

### Goals

| Name       | Text                                                                 | Runtime | Goal Type | Relation | Justification                                                                 |
|------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|---------|-----------|----------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| G1         | Collect and Deliver Required Resources                                  | -       | Achieve  | -        | The mission aims to achieve the state where resources are collected and delivered. |
| G2         | Collect Resources from Various Storages                                | #       | Perform  | AND      | Collection and delivery are both necessary for the mission to succeed.          |
| G3         | Deliver Collected Resources to the Specified Location                  | #       | Perform  | AND      | Both collection and delivery are required phases.                              |
| G2.1       | Collect Resource from Storage A                                        | -       | Perform  | OR       | Multiple collection tasks can be performed in parallel.                        |
| G2.2       | Collect Resource from Storage B                                        | -       | Perform  | OR       | Each storage is a separate task but contributes to the overall collection.     |
| G3.1       | Deliver Resource from Storage A to Destination                        | -       | Perform  | OR       | Multiple delivery tasks can be performed in parallel.                          |
| G3.2       | Deliver Resource from Storage B to Destination                        | -       | Perform  | OR       | Each delivery task is independent but contributes to the overall mission.       |

### Tasks

| Name       | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location                  | Number of Robots | Justification                                                                 |
|------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|---------------------------|------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| AT1.1      | Collect Resource from Storage A                                        | AND      | Sterile Facility A       | 1                | Single robot assigned per storage for efficiency.                            |
| AT1.2      | Collect Resource from Storage B                                        | AND      | Laundry Facility B       | 1                | Each storage requires a dedicated robot for collection.                      |
| AT2.1      | Deliver Resource from Storage A to Destination                        | AND      | Destination Location      | 1                | Each delivery task is handled by a single robot for precision.                |
| AT2.2      | Deliver Resource from Storage B to Destination                        | AND      | Destination Location      | 1                | Ensures each resource is delivered accurately.                               |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**
  - Justification: Both collection and delivery are essential phases for the mission to be completed.

- **G2 -> AT1.1, AT1.2 [OR]**
  - Justification: Multiple resources can be collected in parallel by different robots, enhancing efficiency.

- **G3 -> AT2.1, AT2.2 [OR]**
  - Justification: Deliveries can be executed in parallel, reducing the overall mission time.

This model ensures that the mission is decomposed into manageable tasks, allowing for efficient resource allocation and execution.
